---
# The git-owned config plane, shipped from roles/k8s/home-assistant per slice-5 D3 —
# that role stays the authoring home (validate-ha-config, the macro tests, the skills all
# anchor there); this manifest only carries its files into the cluster. lookup('file'), not
# 'template': every file here is copied verbatim by contract, and 'file' makes a regression
# to real templating fail the deploy loudly. validate_ha_config.py also rejects an Ansible
# marker in the three files an operator would reach for a var in (configuration.yaml,
# customize.yaml, ui-lovelace.yaml): lookup('file') would ship it literally and HA renders an
# unknown name to an empty string without an error.
#
# One ConfigMap per tree, each carrying exactly the files its list in defaults/main.yml
# names. The lists are the single source of what ships: the init container in
# deployment.yaml.j2 installs whatever each ConfigMap holds, and validate_ha_config.py fails
# when a list and its directory disagree, so a file that validates clean cannot silently
# stay out of the pod. Listed rather than globbed because a glob that shipped nothing would
# surface only as missing automations at runtime.
#
# The init container installs these into the /config PVC on every pod start. Runtime-owned
# state (.storage/, the recorder DB, custom_components/) lives only on the PVC and is never
# touched. The ConfigMap names predate the loop and stay as they are: kubectl apply does not
# delete an object it stops declaring, so a rename would leave the old ConfigMap live.
#
# The (ConfigMap, subdirectory) pairing appears once more, in deployment.yaml.j2's volumes.
{% set config_trees = [
     ('home-assistant-config', '', home_assistant_root_files),
     ('home-assistant-automations', 'automations/', home_assistant_automation_files),
     ('home-assistant-scripts', 'scripts/', home_assistant_script_files),
     ('home-assistant-custom-templates', 'custom_templates/', home_assistant_template_files),
   ] %}
{% for configmap_name, subdir, names in config_trees %}
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ configmap_name }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
data:
{% for name in names %}
  {{ name }}: |
{{ lookup('file', playbook_dir + '/roles/k8s/home-assistant/files/' + subdir + name) | indent(4, true) }}
{% endfor %}
{% if not loop.last %}
---
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
